#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# three_j_symbol

#% text
# `three_j_symbol([j1, m1], [j2, m2], [j3, m3])` gives Wigner's 3j symbol, exact; zero outside the selection rules.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
three_j_symbol([1/2, -1/2], [1/2, -1/2], [1, 1])
#% output
#= (-1/3)*3^(1/2)

#% cell
three_j_symbol([2, 1], [2, 2], [4, -3])
#% output
#= (-1/6)*2^(1/2)

